# Netlify SPA fallback — every path serves index.html with HTTP 200
# (NOT a 301/302 redirect, so the URL stays as the user typed it).
# This makes refresh / deep-link work on any client-side route
# handled by src/common/lib/router.tsx.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>
# Docs:   https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# Missing build assets must FAIL, not fall into the SPA rule below. Deploys
# are atomic — a new build deletes the old build's hashed chunks — so an old
# tab lazy-loading a now-deleted /assets/ file would otherwise receive
# index.html with a 200 and die on the "text/html is not a module" MIME check.
# A 404 keeps the failure honest; the vite:preloadError reload (wired in
# src/main.tsx) is what actually recovers. Netlify consults redirects only
# when no real file matches, so live assets are unaffected.
/assets/* /index.html 404
/* /index.html 200
